<title>FRANCE: Rhone-Poulenc Q3 net income rises.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc Q3 net income rises.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to Sept 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net income				     756  vs	     669</p>
<p>    Net income per share (francs)	   2.33  vs	    2.12</p>
<p>    Operating				    2,054  vs	   1,828</p>
<p>    Pre-tax					1,796  vs	   1,751</p>
<p>    Net sales				   20,468  vs	  19,621</p>
<p>    Net interest expense			 552  vs	     332</p>
<p>    Income taxes				   583  vs	     579</p>
<p>    Minorities			     loss  170  vs  loss     217</p>
<p>    Other income				   159  vs	     117</p>
<p>NOTE -- Rhone-Poulenc said in a statement it had taken a charge of 81 million francs for the October recall of Albumin products made by the Cention joint venture.</p>
</text>
